Windows Registry Editor Version 5.00

; ============================================================================
;  HomeFront / Precision Builder — disable the screen-capture "Allow ... to
;  see this tab?" prompt for the Feedback tool (F8 / Shift+F8).
;
;  This pre-authorizes the app's ORIGIN to capture its own browser tab, so the
;  native getDisplayMedia capture runs with NO picker and NO prompt.
;
;  BEFORE IMPORTING:
;    1. Replace  http://localhost:5065  below with the EXACT origin shown in the
;       browser address bar  (scheme + host + port, no path, no trailing slash).
;       Examples:  http://localhost:5065   https://homefront.yourserver.com
;    2. Keep ONLY the section for the browser the testers use (Chrome or Edge);
;       you can leave both — the unused one is harmless.
;    3. Add more origins (different ports / the production URL) as "2", "3", ...
;    4. Double-click this file → Yes (needs admin for HKLM).
;    5. FULLY quit the browser (all windows) and reopen.
;    6. Verify at  chrome://policy  (or edge://policy): TabCaptureAllowedByOrigins
;       should list your origin with status OK ("Reload policies" if needed).
;
;  No admin rights?  Change HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE to HKEY_CURRENT_USER in both keys
;  (Chrome and Edge also read per-user policies).
; ============================================================================

; ---- Google Chrome -------------------------------------------------------
[HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\Policies\Google\Chrome\TabCaptureAllowedByOrigins]
"1"="http://localhost:5065"

; ---- Microsoft Edge ------------------------------------------------------
[HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\Policies\Microsoft\Edge\TabCaptureAllowedByOrigins]
"1"="http://localhost:5065"
